00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:54.380
I believe they're from South
America as opposed to Africa--

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:57.050
they look astonishingly
like ostriches.

00:22:57.050 --> 00:23:01.070
And that was a thing I
was not entirely aware of.

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:04.840
So if I go over here, I can
see a specific precision recall

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.010
curve for this particular label.

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:08.720
And I can see the
list of true positives

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:13.020
that came back for
this particular label.

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:14.690
So these are all
different rheas.

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:16.620
And I can see some of
the false negatives.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:19.070
So this would be photos that
were properly identified

00:23:19.070 --> 00:23:23.360
as rheas but were not above that
0.50 score threshold that I had

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:25.779
specified up here.

00:23:25.779 --> 00:23:28.070
And then down here are some
false positives that I got.

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:33.140
So these are ones where
it was labeled rhea but--

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.180
these are ostrich photos.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:37.810
But we ended up predicting
rhea for whatever reason.

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:40.430
And like in this case, like
this is clearly an ostrich.

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:45.230
But for whatever reason,
the rhea label sort of

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:49.250
edged it out for
whatever reason.

00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:51.890
And that whatever
reason is where

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:57.620
building that intuition around
how this model is working

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.610
starts to allow
these to formulate

00:24:00.610 --> 00:24:02.900
some interesting
follow-up actions on

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:06.112
like, what should they do
next to improve their model?

00:24:06.112 --> 00:24:07.820
So one option that
they could potentially

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:13.170
do is one that we say up
here is that basically,

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:16.440
if you were to add more
images to your data sets,

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:18.750
this would probably allow
you to improve your model.

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:22.060
And if I look at my
label stats, I actually

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:23.810
only uploaded just a
couple hundred images

00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:24.851
for each of these labels.

00:24:24.851 --> 00:24:27.950
And as it turns out
for cassowary and emu,

00:24:27.950 --> 00:24:30.140
I mean, maybe this might
suffice because like it

00:24:30.140 --> 00:24:31.430
seems to perform pretty well.

00:24:31.430 --> 00:24:33.410
But for ostrich,
I had 400 images.

00:24:33.410 --> 00:24:34.910
And for rhea, I
only had 200 images.

00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:36.368
Maybe I should add
more rhea images

00:24:36.368 --> 00:24:40.709
in order to see if I
can get my metrics up.

00:24:40.709 --> 00:24:42.500
Another possibility
that I might want to do

00:24:42.500 --> 00:24:44.359
is just take a look
at these images

00:24:44.359 --> 00:24:45.900
and see maybe I
might have mislabeled

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:46.890
some of these images.

00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:49.780
And so like in this
case, like this one was--

00:24:49.780 --> 00:24:52.850
the ground truth is an ostrich.

00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:54.890
But I think this
is actually a rhea.

00:24:54.890 --> 00:24:59.177
And I think maybe I just went
and mislabeled these images.

00:24:59.177 --> 00:25:01.010
So another thing that
I could potentially do

00:25:01.010 --> 00:25:04.400
is backtrack to the
Images tab over here

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:10.220
and go to my rhea
